The elements of theatre are the basic building blocks, or components, that a theatre maker works with and puts together to make a performance: they are the raw materials of the art form, and any production is a particular selection and arrangement of them. Four of the elements of theatre arts are:
1. plot - the story or the sequence of events that happens on stage;
2. character - the people (or beings) in the drama, with their wants, relationships and conflicts;
3. space - the place and stage area the action uses, including the stage positions and the relationship between the performers and the audience;
4. mood - the atmosphere or feeling of a moment or a scene, which is created by all the other choices working together.
(Other correct elements: theme, dialogue, rhythm, movement, spectacle, audience.)
